{"authored" [{"question" "q-339797" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3{sin}^{2}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/state.json" "file_sha256" "de23134ab4bcd441473ee39e0b42187397413b02908e3a1e42d4b3e99a7610b9" "basis" 1575 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-339797" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that as $x\\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$\n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{3{sin}^{2}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}}=\\frac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form.\n\nInstead, let's recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}=1\n$$\n\nRewriting the given limit using the algebra of limits and applying our special limit, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{3{sin}^{2}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}{(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {[{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}]}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/state.json" "file_sha256" "de23134ab4bcd441473ee39e0b42187397413b02908e3a1e42d4b3e99a7610b9" "basis" 1575 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-339797" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "037a9a81d66e735858297d54854b5d611f47719f226839c9f30fd92ade896351" "basis" 1575 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-339797" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/state.json" "file_sha256" "de23134ab4bcd441473ee39e0b42187397413b02908e3a1e42d4b3e99a7610b9" "basis" 1575 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-340150" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }{4\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/state.json" "file_sha256" "de23134ab4bcd441473ee39e0b42187397413b02908e3a1e42d4b3e99a7610b9" "basis" 1575 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-340150" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we can simplify the limit using trigonometric identities, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }{4\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta } & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }÷4\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }÷\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{4}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{4}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate the limits separately:\n\n- Consider the first limit. Notice that as $\\theta \\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$ \n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form. \n\nRewriting the given limit using the algebra of limits and applying our special limit, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{1}{({lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta })} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider the second limit. Evaluating it directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{4}=\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡0}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{4} & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/state.json" "file_sha256" "de23134ab4bcd441473ee39e0b42187397413b02908e3a1e42d4b3e99a7610b9" "basis" 1575 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-340150" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "037a9a81d66e735858297d54854b5d611f47719f226839c9f30fd92ade896351" "basis" 1575 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-340150" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/state.json" "file_sha256" "de23134ab4bcd441473ee39e0b42187397413b02908e3a1e42d4b3e99a7610b9" "basis" 1575 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-340150" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/state.json" "file_sha256" "de23134ab4bcd441473ee39e0b42187397413b02908e3a1e42d4b3e99a7610b9" "basis" 1575 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-94" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to 0}\\: \\dfrac{2\\sin{x}}{3x} .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/example-94.json" "file_sha256" "7b73def64447d60c8e141507ffe97b26c110ee2222dfb50216b320f1ba4d73ec" "basis" 1575 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-94" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that as $x \\to 0,$ both the numerator and denominator approach $0.$\n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to 0}\\: \\dfrac{2\\sin{x}}{3x} = \\dfrac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form.\n\nInstead, let's recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to 0}\\: \\dfrac{\\sin{x}}{x} = 1\n$$\n\nRewriting the given limit using the algebra of limits and applying our special limit, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{3x} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/example-94.json" "file_sha256" "7b73def64447d60c8e141507ffe97b26c110ee2222dfb50216b320f1ba4d73ec" "basis" 1575 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\lim_\\limits{\\theta \\to 0}\\: \\dfrac{\\theta \\cot \\theta}{4 \\cos^2 \\theta}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/example-6167.json" "file_sha256" "fbba6d737e2af37f0430f5887865eaeac057d38ae3fd7ed19c0bf34d69eab87c" "basis" 1575 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-6167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we can simplify the limit using trigonometric identities, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }{4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta } & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\theta }{4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\theta }{4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate the limits separately:\n\n- Consider the first limit. Notice that as $\\theta \\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$ \n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{\\theta \\to 0}\\: \\dfrac{\\theta}{\\sin\\theta} = \\dfrac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form. \n\nRewriting the given limit using the algebra of limits and applying our special limit, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{1}{({lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta })} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider the second limit. Evaluating it directly, we get\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{\\theta \\to 0} \\:\\dfrac{1}{4 \\cos \\theta} = \\dfrac{1}{4\\cos 0} = \\dfrac14.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/example-6167.json" "file_sha256" "fbba6d737e2af37f0430f5887865eaeac057d38ae3fd7ed19c0bf34d69eab87c" "basis" 1575 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14042622/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-339797" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3{sin}^{2}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-339797" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that as $x\\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$\n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{3{sin}^{2}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}}=\\frac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form.\n\nInstead, let's recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}=1\n$$\n\nRewriting the given limit using the algebra of limits and applying our special limit, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{3{sin}^{2}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}{(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {[{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}]}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-339797" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bee430c540c9fd61b34b052c76fb613c9f3db6c17f95b4b8c90a310b6a5600ba"} {"question" "q-339797" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-339797" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-339798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{sin}^{5}⁡x}{4{x}^{4}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-339798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that as $x\\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$\n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{{sin}^{5}⁡x}{4{x}^{4}}=\\frac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form.\n\nInstead, let's recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}=1\n$$\n\nRewriting the given limit using the algebra of limits and applying our special limit, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{{sin}^{5}⁡x}{4{x}^{4}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{4}⁡x}{{x}^{4}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{{sin}^{4}⁡x}{{x}^{4}}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}{(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x})}^{4}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {[{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}]}^{4}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot {1}^{4}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-339798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bee430c540c9fd61b34b052c76fb613c9f3db6c17f95b4b8c90a310b6a5600ba"} {"question" "q-339798" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-339798" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-339692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,(-\\frac{21\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4x})=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-339692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that as $x\\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$\n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{21\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4x}=\\frac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form.\n\nInstead, let's recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}=1\n$$\n\nRewriting the given limit using the algebra of limits and applying our special limit, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,(\\frac{21\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{4x}) & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(-\\frac{21}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{21}{4}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{21}{4}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{21}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-339692" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bee430c540c9fd61b34b052c76fb613c9f3db6c17f95b4b8c90a310b6a5600ba"} {"question" "q-339692" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-339692" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{21}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-4487" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{x}{7\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-4487" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that as $x\\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$\n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{x}{7\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=\\frac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form.\n\nInstead, let's recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}=1\n$$\n\nRewriting the given limit using the algebra of limits and applying our special limit, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{x}{7\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot \\frac{x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}{(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x})}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot {[{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot {1}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-4487" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bee430c540c9fd61b34b052c76fb613c9f3db6c17f95b4b8c90a310b6a5600ba"} {"question" "q-4487" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-4487" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{7}"] ["math" "\\text{DNE}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-4487" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{7}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-105409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{4{sin}^{2}⁡x}{5{x}^{2}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-105409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that as $x\\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$\n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{4{sin}^{2}⁡x}{5{x}^{2}}=\\frac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form.\n\nInstead, let's recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}=1\n$$\n\nRewriting the given limit using the algebra of limits and applying our special limit, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{4{sin}^{2}⁡x}{5{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot \\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡x}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}{(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot {[{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}]}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot {1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-105409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bee430c540c9fd61b34b052c76fb613c9f3db6c17f95b4b8c90a310b6a5600ba"} {"question" "q-105409" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-105409" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{16}{25}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{5}"] ["math" "\\text{DNE}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-105409" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-340150" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }{4\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-340150" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we can simplify the limit using trigonometric identities, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }{4\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta } & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }÷4\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }÷\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{4}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{4}) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate the limits separately:\n\n- Consider the first limit. Notice that as $\\theta \\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$ \n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form. \n\nRewriting the given limit using the algebra of limits and applying our special limit, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{1}{({lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta })} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider the second limit. Evaluating it directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{4}=\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡0}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{4} & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-340150" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bee430c540c9fd61b34b052c76fb613c9f3db6c17f95b4b8c90a310b6a5600ba"} {"question" "q-340150" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-340150" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-73548" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of ${lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta }.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-73548" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we can simplify the limit using trigonometric identities, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta } & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta ÷\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }÷\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that as $\\theta \\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$\n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form.\n\nInstead, let's recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }=1\n$$\n\nRewriting the given limit using the algebra of limits and applying our special limit, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}{(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta })}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }]}^{-1} \\\\  & ={1}^{-1} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-73548" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bee430c540c9fd61b34b052c76fb613c9f3db6c17f95b4b8c90a310b6a5600ba"} {"question" "q-73548" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-73548" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-73548" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-340137" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1}{3\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-340137" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we can simplify the limit using trigonometric identities, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{{sec}^{2}⁡\\theta -1}{3\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{{tan}^{2}⁡\\theta }{3\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{(\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta })}{3\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{3\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{3{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta }) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{1}{3{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate the limits separately:\n\n- Consider the first limit. Notice that as $\\theta \\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$ \n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }=\\frac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form. \n\nInstead, let's recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta } & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider the second limit. Evaluating it directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{1}{3{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{1}{3{cos}^{4}⁡0}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta })\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{1}{3{cos}^{4}⁡\\theta } & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-340137" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bee430c540c9fd61b34b052c76fb613c9f3db6c17f95b4b8c90a310b6a5600ba"} {"question" "q-340137" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-340137" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-105426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\theta \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta }=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-105426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we can simplify the limit using trigonometric identities, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\theta \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta } & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }÷\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }÷\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate the limits separately:\n\n- Consider the first limit. Notice that as $\\theta \\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$ \n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form. \n\nInstead, let's recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider the second limit. Evaluating it directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =1\\cdot 1=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-105426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bee430c540c9fd61b34b052c76fb613c9f3db6c17f95b4b8c90a310b6a5600ba"} {"question" "q-105426" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-105426" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\text{DNE}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-105426" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-302827" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-302827" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we can simplify the limit using trigonometric identities, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{\\theta } & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }}{\\theta } \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate the limits separately:\n\n- Consider the first limit. Notice that as $\\theta \\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$ \n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }=\\frac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form. \n\nInstead, let's recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }=1\n$$\n\n- Consider the second limit. Evaluating it directly, we get\n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡0}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\frac{1}{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta } & =1\\cdot 1=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta }{\\theta }=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-302827" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "bee430c540c9fd61b34b052c76fb613c9f3db6c17f95b4b8c90a310b6a5600ba"} {"question" "q-302827" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "q-302827" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/state.json" "file_sha256" "653a97abcf591d6036feaa6884f2f5550659d189b5b1c2727dd1f4ffc6b4c881"} {"question" "e-94" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to 0}\\: \\dfrac{2\\sin{x}}{3x} .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/example-94.json" "file_sha256" "7b73def64447d60c8e141507ffe97b26c110ee2222dfb50216b320f1ba4d73ec"} {"question" "e-94" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that as $x \\to 0,$ both the numerator and denominator approach $0.$\n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to 0}\\: \\dfrac{2\\sin{x}}{3x} = \\dfrac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form.\n\nInstead, let's recall the following special limit:\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to 0}\\: \\dfrac{\\sin{x}}{x} = 1\n$$\n\nRewriting the given limit using the algebra of limits and applying our special limit, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{3x} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/example-94.json" "file_sha256" "7b73def64447d60c8e141507ffe97b26c110ee2222dfb50216b320f1ba4d73ec"} {"question" "e-6167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\lim_\\limits{\\theta \\to 0}\\: \\dfrac{\\theta \\cot \\theta}{4 \\cos^2 \\theta}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/example-6167.json" "file_sha256" "fbba6d737e2af37f0430f5887865eaeac057d38ae3fd7ed19c0bf34d69eab87c"} {"question" "e-6167" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we can simplify the limit using trigonometric identities, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta }{4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta } & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\theta }{4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\theta }{4{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}(\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }) \\\\  & ={lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate the limits separately:\n\n- Consider the first limit. Notice that as $\\theta \\to 0,$ both numerator and denominator approach $0.$ \n\nSo, if we attempt to evaluate the limit directly, we get\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{\\theta \\to 0}\\: \\dfrac{\\theta}{\\sin\\theta} = \\dfrac{0}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is an indeterminate form. \n\nRewriting the given limit using the algebra of limits and applying our special limit, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{1}{({lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\theta })} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider the second limit. Evaluating it directly, we get\n\n$$\n\\lim_\\limits{\\theta \\to 0} \\:\\dfrac{1}{4 \\cos \\theta} = \\dfrac{1}{4\\cos 0} = \\dfrac14.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {lim}_{\\theta \\to 0}\\,\\frac{1}{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } & =1\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076663/example-6167.json" "file_sha256" "fbba6d737e2af37f0430f5887865eaeac057d38ae3fd7ed19c0bf34d69eab87c"}] "usage" {"q-339797" [] "q-4487" [] "e-94" [] "e-6167" [] "q-340150" []} "basis" 2781 "retractions" [[17592186078851 :question/problem "What is $lim_(x → 0)\\frac{x}{7\\sin x}$?"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186076318 17592186076319 17592186076320 17592186076321 17592186076322 17592186317511 17592186317512 17592186317519] "immutable_fields" [[17592186076317 :answer-field/correct] [17592186076317 :answer-field/id] [17592186076317 :answer-field/key] [17592186076317 :answer-field/type] [17592186317510 :answer-field/correct] [17592186317510 :answer-field/id] [17592186317510 :answer-field/key] [17592186317510 :answer-field/type] [17592186317518 :answer-field/correct] [17592186317518 :answer-field/id] [17592186317518 :answer-field/key] [17592186317518 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
